## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of PIM for cross-tenant vendor access scenarios; validates understanding of governance, auditability, and emergency access controls in real-world incident response environments.

## Key Concepts
- Privileged Identity Management (PIM)
- Eligible vs Active assignments
- Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
- Approval workflows
- Just-in-time activation
- Conditional Access integration
- Audit logging and monitoring
- Automatic revocation mechanisms
- Cross-tenant access patterns
- Time-bound access controls
- Compliance reporting

## Code Example
```javascript
// PIM activation request configuration
const pimRequest = {
  roleId: 'incident-admin-role',
  justification: 'Critical incident response - vendor access required',
  duration: 'PT4H', // 4 hours maximum
  ticketInfo: {
    system: 'ServiceNow',
    ticketId: 'INC001234',
    ticketUrl: 'https://company.service-now.com/incident'
  },
  approvers: ['security-team@company.com'],
  mfaRequired: true,
  activationType: 'just-in-time'
};

// Monitor PIM activation logs
function monitorPIMActivations() {
  return {
    startTime: '2024-01-15T10:00:00Z',
    endTime: '2024-01-15T14:00:00Z',
    filters: {
      activity: 'Activate',
      targetResources: ['incident-portal-app'],
      initiatedBy: 'external-vendors'
    }
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical Conditional Access implementation skills for a new administrator working with external users, emphasizing safe deployment and validation procedures.

## Key Concepts
- Conditional Access fundamentals: MFA requirements, device compliance enforcement, IP-based restrictions
- Application targeting and scope management using security groups
- Pilot rollout methodology with validation and rollback procedures

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Azure CLI/Graph example for policy configuration
const policy = {
  displayName: 'ContractorPortal-CA',
  conditions: {
    users: { includeGroups: ['Contractors'] },
    applications: { includeApplications: ['InternalPortal'] },
    clientAppTypes: ['browser', 'mobileAppsAndDesktopClients']
  },
  grantControls: {
    operator: 'OR',
    builtInControls: ['mfa', 'compliantDevice', 'domainJoinedDevice']
  },
  sessionControls: {
    persistentBrowserMode: 'never'
  }
};
```

## Implementation Notes
- Start with report-only mode to assess impact before enforcement
- Use Azure AD sign-in logs for real-time monitoring during pilot
- Document exceptions and create escalation procedures for access issues
